From 30c750f0bd89602f7e76db93bbb81c9aa8e58238 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:31:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Read the yt3d keywords with libstereo-policy

The edition has one reader of YouTube's yt3d keywords, in libstereo-policy
(stereo_policy_site_mark), which its browser uses too. PlasmaTube calls it
instead of keeping a table of the tags.

The reader takes the first form, yt3d:enable=true, as right eye first, as
YouTube's player did (it showed a parallel video right only with
yt3d:swap=true), so yt3d:swap=true makes it left eye first: this reverses
the order the first patch gave these two tags, which showed "3D Maestro"
(enable=true, swap=true) with its eyes swapped. The rectangles are read
numerically ("Kate in 3D!" has left=0_0._0.5_1), and rectangles beat the
first form's side by side.

Depends on libstereo-policy1 (>= 1.13.0) and builds against
libstereo-policy-dev.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
